ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-key-here

# On Bedrock instead? Comment out the line above and set these two:
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=...
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# In the workshop, your facilitator gives the room one key for the session. It is only for
# the progress checks, /catchup and the client review in session two (Claude Code runs
# on your own Claude access), and it
# stops working once the session is over. Copy it on
# the build site: the box "Your key to Claude" in Setting up, Part 3, or
# Menu -> Copy your key to Claude. Then run  python3 setup.py --key  in your own terminal
# and paste it: that writes .env for you, and the key never shows on screen.
# If the box says the key is not released yet, ask your facilitator.

# Already signed in with `ant auth login`? You don't need this file at all:
# see support/client.py for the resolution order.

# Apart from the workshop key above, one key per person, never a shared team key:
# a key in a file two people edit is a key that ends up in a commit. Copy this to .env (which is gitignored),
# and if a key ever reaches the repo, rotate it and tell a facilitator.
